Z||000000||Manta||08-16-2000||12:47 AM||||Just wondering if anyone knows how you can tell the difference between the 86 and 86 ½ Fiero G.T.s.<BR>Also how many 86 ½ Fiero G.Ts. were made.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||08-16-2000||03:18 AM||||12,742 Fiero GT's made in 1986.<BR>The 86 1/2 GT is the same as an 86 GT. They call it 86 1/2 because they came out later in the year with the fastback body. There is no 86 GT notchback.||||reg||1
Z||000002||gtsonly||08-16-2000||03:29 AM||||plus the 86.5 had the beefed up suspension (cititaion instead of chevette) and the tranny. early 86's had a 4 speed, midyear 86's got the getrag 5 speed. and yes the fastback too!!!<BR>  chris hatch||||reg||14
Z||000003||Oreif||08-16-2000||03:48 AM||||gtsonly, The front of a fiero IS a chevette suspension and the rear IS a citation suspension. This is the same for 84 thru 87 Fiero's. The Getreg 5spds were only in the last 2 months of build in 1986. an 86 GT is the same exact car as an 86.5 GT.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||08-16-2000||04:00 AM||||When someone says 86.5 GT, they're usually refering to an 86 GT that has the Getrag 5 speed.  There is no such thing as a notchback 86 GT..<P>There were about 2,200 86 GT's that came with the getrag, so it is one of the rarer models  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 149,000 miles and counting!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||86SE||08-16-2000||04:25 AM||||How many 86SE's were made?  I have one of the lasts ones made in 86, within the last 1000 I think.....<P>How many 86SE's with autos were made?<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Stering wheel<BR>Gas AND brake petals<BR>**Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention**||||reg||5
Z||000006||stimpy||08-16-2000||06:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>When someone says 86.5 GT, they're usually refering to an 86 GT that has the Getrag 5 speed.  There is no such thing as a notchback 86 GT..<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Orief is correct- ALL GT's in 86 are 86 1/2, just like all 64 Mustangs are 64 1/2. Since they are introduced <B>after</B> the rest of the product line, so called "mid-year" models often get the "1/2" suffix. Nope, it doesn't make it any more rare, doesn't mean it has different suspension/engine/tranny/trim. Just means it's an 86.<P>Oh wait, isn't 86 1/2 when they first tried the lotus suspension? hehehehe <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||trigger||08-16-2000||09:23 AM||||Hi,<BR>If the 84-87 had the citation/ celebrity suspension, then what was the 88 suspension off of?  Was it all by itself or was it off some other car?  Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||08-16-2000||10:51 AM||||The 88 suspension was by itself. It was redesigned for the car "based" on a Lotus style set-up (read ~ not designed by Lotus but based on the same geometry of how the suspension is set-up. Lotus had Nothing to do with the 88 suspension.)<BR>11,961 SE's were made in 1986<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||08-16-2000||03:10 PM||||The Fiero does not have the Citation front suspension. They are different. It has the GM FWD suspension "design" adapted to the rear. Turns out the X/A/G have essentially the same thing. Is it a Ceira suspension? Lesabre? No.<P>Same for the front. <P>Calling them the "Chevette" and "Citation" suspension is great if the goal is to attach some negative connatation to the quality, but in fact, they aren't the same thing.<P>The above was pretty much what one of the Pontiac engineers told me. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 08-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Standard||08-16-2000||11:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B> Orief is correct- ALL GT's in 86 are 86 1/2 </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know they didn't start making them till mid-year, but I generally refer to 86 GT's as 86 GT's, unless they have the 5 speed, then I call them 86.5's.. just an easier way to differentiate i guess.. if you wanna get <B>real</B> technical i guess you could call the 5 speed GT's 86 3/4's..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 149,000 miles and counting!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||2birds||08-17-2000||01:55 AM||||Mine has a build date of June 12, 1986, and has a Getrag.  I've also seen other 86 fastbacks with 4-speeds, so I don't think the 4 speed and fastback are mutually exclusive, but they are close to doing so.  Seems to me that a 4-speed fastback would be the rarest, but I-d rather have my 5-speed.<P>As far as the origin of the suspenions, I'm happy that the ball joints, window motors,  and countless other parts are shared with other GM designs.  Makes buying new parts a little easier on the wallet.||||reg||1
Z||000012||mdjoneses||08-17-2000||06:14 AM||||My buddy wanted the 86GT IN January 1986. They were not available so he ordered 86SE loaded which I bought from him July 1987.  Mark||||reg||1
Z||000013||anthony_86gt||02-14-2001||08:35 PM||||i have an 86.5gt. how much quicker is the gts than the SEs and regulars.  ||||reg||1
Z||000014||ray b||02-14-2001||09:16 PM||||gt 's are slower  and heaver than seV6's.<BR>4speeds are faster than 5speeds in 1/4 esp 4.10 rears||||reg||1
Z||000015||Standard||02-15-2001||02:36 AM||||No v6 car came stock with a 4.10, and they're horrible for highway driving anyways.  85 and most 86 V6 cars came with the 3.65 ratio 4 speed.  Stock for stock, the GT should only be around .1 sec slower.  5 speed has better gear ratios, so that'll help even more.||||reg||1
Z||000016||lou_dias||02-15-2001||09:14 AM||||the 4 speed v6's had a 3.61 axle gear ratio,<BR>the 5 speed v6's had a 3.65||||reg||1
